# Privacy Policy — Bleed

**Effective date:** [date]

This policy explains what data the Discord bot **Bleed** collects, stores, and does not collect.

## 1. What We Do Not Collect

Bleed does **not** collect, store, or process any of the following:

- IP addresses
- Geolocation or location data
- Hardware identifiers (HWID) or device fingerprints
- Cookies
- Third-party analytics or advertising trackers

No third-party services are embedded in the bot or on the associated website for the purpose of tracking users.

## 2. What Is Stored

Only the minimum data required to operate in a server is retained:

- Server-specific configuration you explicitly set, such as custom prefixes, aliases, logging settings, or similar preferences.
- This data is stored locally and is not shared with third parties.

## 3. The Website

The Terms of Service / Privacy Policy page is static. It embeds no external resources, sets no cookies, and collects nothing from visitors.

## 4. Data Retention & Deletion

Data is retained only as long as needed to provide the features you have configured. Removing the bot from a server and/or contacting the operators (see below) to request deletion will stop further collection and result in removal of stored server configuration where technically feasible.

## 5. Third-Party Services

Discord itself processes data according to Discord's own [Privacy Policy](https://discord.com/privacy). Use of Bleed is subject to Discord's terms in addition to this policy.

## 6. Changes to This Policy

This policy may be updated from time to time. Continued use after an update constitutes acceptance of the revised policy. The effective date above reflects the most recent revision.

## 7. Contact

For privacy questions or deletion requests, contact the operators through **[contact method]**.

---

This policy applies only to the bot Bleed and does not modify Discord's own Privacy Policy.
